      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the late 1880s, the Chicago, Burlington & Quincy Railroad ran through Atwood, spurring its growth as an agricultural hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/atwood-kansas/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Atwood became the county seat of Rawlins County in 1881, a status it holds to this day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atwood%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Visitors can explore the Rawlins County Historical Museum, the historic Shirley Opera House, or relax by Lake Atwood just north of town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/atwood-kansas/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
